Third-party components and data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This project depends on the following open-source software (installed via their
own package managers, not redistributed here):

  - @modelcontextprotocol/sdk  — MIT License
  - dotenv                     — BSD-2-Clause License

The Python tools invoked at runtime (run_pymatgen and related) expect a
user-provided scientific Python stack, which is licensed separately by its
authors, including but not limited to:

  - pymatgen      — MIT License
  - ASE (Atomic Simulation Environment) — LGPL-2.1-or-later
  - NumPy / SciPy / spglib — BSD-style licenses

These packages are NOT bundled with this repository; users install them
themselves.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pseudopotential / parameter data
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Recommended cutoff and pseudopotential metadata under server/knowledge and
server/src/tools/data is derived from the Standard Solid-State Pseudopotentials
(SSSP) library:

  G. Prandini, A. Marrazzo, I. E. Castelli, N. Mounet and N. Marzari,
  npj Computational Materials 4, 72 (2018). https://www.materialscloud.org/sssp

Default Hubbard U values bundled under server/src/tools (lookup_hubbard_u) are
taken from the Materials Project calibration:

  L. Wang, T. Maxisch and G. Ceder, Phys. Rev. B 73, 195107 (2006).

The search_materials tool queries the Materials Project, AFLOW and OQMD public
databases over HTTP using the user's own API key; their data is not bundled or
redistributed in this repository. Materials Project: https://materialsproject.org

Actual pseudopotential (.UPF) files and VASP POTCAR files are NOT included and
must be obtained by the user from their respective sources under their own
licenses (e.g. SSSP / Materials Cloud for QE; VASP POTCARs require a VASP
license from the VASP group).

